card.statement:
If $\{T_j\}_{j\in\Z}$ is a set of commuting elements
of an algebra with at most finitely many nonzero elements, then
for all $j,k\in\Z$ the following identities hold:

\begin{align}
\sum_{i\in\Z\setminus I(k-j)} (-1)^{\delta_{i<0}} T_{j+i}T_{k-i} &= -\delta_{j>k} T_jT_k,\\
\sum_{i\in\Z\setminus I(-1+k-j)} (-1)^{\delta_{i<0}} T_{j+i}T_{k-i} &=\delta_{j<k} T_jT_k,
\end{align}

where $I(k)$ was defined in <<ref:eq:I_def>>.
